      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>In our group, there's often a resistance to setting a game in a preestablished fictional setting (like Marvel, Dresden Files, Star Trek, etc) because depending on the setting, there will be people who know a lot of the lore vs those who don't. And while it hasn't seemed to come up when we play in published RPG settings like Golarian or Torg, that \"I don't get that reference\" thing seems to be a bigger deal.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>That said, when I run one-shots, it's always with canon characters and folks have a good time.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I honestly don't know how folks will feel about playing in the Sentinel Comics setting vs an original super-setting.&nbsp;</p>",
